        <mxCell id="JgXxKuTrH8b0v2rZ6a8R-38" value="The pipeline will continue.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;The new &lt;u&gt;column&#39;s name&lt;/u&gt; is stored inside an Azure Blob called &lt;b&gt;new_columns.json&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;, alongside the &lt;u&gt;date&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The backfill pipeline will add it later. For this to happen, we must therefore specify the column name inside &lt;b&gt;tables_schema.py&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="shape=hexagon;perimeter=hexagonPerimeter2;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fixedSize=1;sketch=1;curveFitting=1;jiggle=2;rounded=0;shadow=0;align=left;spacingRight=5;spacingLeft=20;fontSize=12;horizontal=1;fontFamily=Comic Sans MS;" vertex="1" parent="1">
